`ls` learns two things of Dukovo's own (ADR 0442), neither of which
changes what GNU's ls prints into a pipe unless it is asked for:

- `--app`: in the long listing, a column with the app each file belongs
  to and how: sealed inside an installed bundle, not sealed inside one
  that is not, data in its app-data folder, temp in its /tmp folder, or
  `-`. The app's name comes only from a sealed bundle's manifest, made
  safe to show; otherwise it is the bundle's ID.
- `--subvolumes[=WHEN]`: `[subvolume]` or `[subvolume, read-only]` after
  each folder of the long listing that is the top of a Btrfs subvolume,
  on a terminal unless WHEN says otherwise.

The code is in apps.rs and subvolumes.rs; display.rs writes the column
and the marks, and fields.rs gives them colours. Dukovo only. Applies
after 0010.

